60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Looking at our options, Plan A, the Market Plaza, seems the most rational. It prioritizes hard-surfacing, which we know is cheaper to maintain and more durable than the ""architectural mirages"" of greenery.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Plan A minimizes deep excavation and complex earth-works, reducing the risk of slippage and delays. It also seems the most feasible to implement without causing total chaos at the main gate.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm with you guys! Plan A sounds perfect because it's mostly paved. Since planted areas cost triple to keep up, a plaza is way safer for our budget. It won't become a money pit!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, I agree. Plan A is the only viable option. Plans B and C require intensive gardening and ecological management that our seven remaining staff members simply cannot provide. We cannot risk further straining the rota.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, I agree. Plan A is the most resilient choice. It accommodates the heavy pedestrian flow to the tram without destroying margins and avoids the drainage and heat issues that would plague the more organic designs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It is quite refreshing to see such a swift consensus. We have collectively decided that a paved plaza is preferable to a woodland or wetland that would inevitably succumb to neglect and budget cuts.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Plan D's terraces would likely require significant earth-moving and structural support, which is too risky given the clay subsoil. Plan A is the only one that truly respects the site's physical and logistical constraints.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,Exactly! Plan D sounds like it would be a nightmare to build and probably expensive to keep up too. Plan A is just so much simpler and safer for everyone. I'm totally voting for the Market Plaza!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, I agree. Plan A is the only choice that doesn't assume a workforce we don't have. It is the only plan that is realistically manageable with our current staffing levels. I will vote for Plan A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,I agree. Plan A is the only option that acknowledges the reality of the site. It provides the firm ground the public already seeks and avoids the drainage failures inherent in the other designs. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have reached a rare and efficient unanimity. Plan A is the only candidate that avoids the pitfalls of high-maintenance greenery and structural instability. I shall cast my vote for the Market Plaza.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. Plan A is the most pragmatic choice, avoiding the risks of clay subsoil and ensuring a manageable construction phase. I will also cast my vote for the Market Plaza.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we're all on the same page! Plan A is definitely the way to go to keep the city's finances happy. I'm voting for the Market Plaza too!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,The logic is sound. Plan A is the only option that does not rely on a phantom workforce. To choose any other would be to set the remaining staff up for failure. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,The evidence is clear. Plan A is the only option that aligns with the actual behavior of the people and the land. It is the most sustainable and realistic choice. I vote for Plan A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure to conclude a committee meeting with such absolute clarity. We have chosen the path of durability over the path of delusion. I concur with the final tally.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. By prioritizing stability and feasibility over aesthetic ambition, we have ensured a result that the city can actually deliver and maintain. I concur with the final decision.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,Yay! I'm so happy we found a plan that's actually doable and won't cause any budget scares later. The Market Plaza is definitely the winner! I concur with the final decision!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Asuka,,The decision is logical and based on the available data. We have avoided a plan that would be impossible to maintain with our current staffing. I concur with the final decision.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I concur. We have based our decision on the physical and operational realities of the park, ensuring the final result is functional and sustainable. I support the selection of Plan A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
